  "limitations": "Square nonnegative dense matrix of 1..32 vertices. Directed input is deliberately averaged with its transpose: this loses orientation. No graph inference, eigensolver, Fourier basis, negative-edge model or graph learning. Self-loop handling follows D-W / normalized formula.",
  "port_notes": "Ports Graph.compute_laplacian combinatorial and normalized formulas using dense Python lists, with directed mean-symmetrization and zero normalized diagonal for isolated vertices. Weighted degrees come from the symmetrized matrix.",
